        "original_id": "22613f23-65b7-5489-aa91-dce10f8f48d3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Keith Morris, Rome Ramirez, Eric Wilson, Josh Freese\n- Bands: Black Flag, Circle Jerks, Off!, Sublime with Rome, Sublime, The Vandals, Dirty Heads\n- Songs: \"We've Had Enough\", \"Lay Me Down\"\n- Genres: hardcore punk, reggae rock\n- Places: Fremont, California\n- Charts: Billboard Alternative Songs, Billboard Rock Songs\n\nFacts:\n- Keith Morris was born on September 18, 1955.\n- Keith Morris is an American singer and songwriter.\n- Keith Morris was the frontman of the hardcore punk bands Black Flag, Circle Jerks, and Off!.\n- Rome Ramirez was born as Roman René Ramírez on June 11, 1988, in Fremont, California.\n- Rome Ramirez is an American singer and guitarist.\n- Rome Ramirez is best known for playing in Sublime with Rome with Eric Wilson from Sublime and Josh Freese from The Vandals.\n- \"We've Had Enough\" features backing vocals by Keith Morris.\n- Keith Morris was the singer of Circle Jerks and the original singer of Black Flag.\n- The 2010 song \"Lay Me Down\" by Dirty Heads featuring Rome Ramirez helped boost the popularity of reggae rock.\n- \"Lay Me Down\" reached number 1 on the Billboard Alternative Songs and Billboard Rock Songs charts.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
